Original commit body from 3c3dc97772eac10d115a3815e3b6feb382fe28d2:

js_package_entry.probe_file tried base_path.with_suffix(ext) for each
probe extension. Path.with_suffix REPLACES the last dotted segment, so
`import { AlbumWrapper } from './Album.test-wrapper'` became Album.tsx -- an
existing, different file -- and a dotted name with no same-stem sibling
(`./cli/help.spec`, `../mocks/hls.mock`, `./dashboard.meta`) resolved to
nothing. Node APPENDS the extension. Found by the WI-halol shape-5
precision audit re-run on merged dev: 30 of 3,890 relative resolutions
bound to the wrong sibling, all nuclear.

probe_file now tries the path, then the path with each extension
appended, then -- only for a specifier ending in a JS extension -- its TS
twin (`./x.js` -> x.ts, .jsx -> .tsx, .mjs -> .mts, .cjs -> .cts:
TypeScript's ESM convention, which the replacement had given by accident),
then the directory's index. The linker and js_ts's default-export
resolver share this function.

Measured, js-module-linker edges, branch vs merged dev 2613b61e34: nuclear
36 removed (every `*.test-wrapper` import bound to the component, and the
module_exports derived from those wrong files) and 53 added (the wrapper
files, `*.meta`, `*.test.data`, `log-stories.data`); knex 9 added
(`require('./cli/help.spec')` ...); hls.js 10 added (`../../mocks/hls.mock`
...); apollo-server 0. Every edge read against its import line.

Tests (test_js_module_linker.py): a dotted basename beside a same-stem
file; a dotted basename with no file names nothing; ./x.js / ./y.jsx /
./z.mjs still name their TS sources; ./styles.css is not swapped. Two
mutations (replace the suffix again, no TS twin) each turn a test red.

Addresses WI-dunab; unblocks WI-halol's shape-5 grant.

